Subject: icnss2: Samsung /sys/wifi interface for macloader (SM-A528B)

Port of CONFIG_SEC_SS_CNSS_FEATURE_SYSFS from the phone's 5.4 icnss2
(drivers/soc/qcom/icnss2/{main,qmi}.c). The closed vendor macloader writes
/sys/wifi/{mac_addr,ant,pm} and reads wifiver, softap, qcwlanstate, wificable.
mac_addr -> cnss_utils provisioned MAC (the phone's DT has no use-nv-mac);
ant 1/2/10 -> board file bdwlan.elf<N>; firmware-ready waits up to 10 s for
the MAC write, as on 5.4. Built with CONFIG_SEC_SS_CNSS_FEATURE_SYSFS=y.
Changes vs 5.4: own file, gpiod API, sysfs_emit, input validation, a mutex
around the info strings. Exports cnss_sysfs_update_driver_status() and
cnss_sysfs_get_pm_info() for the WLAN host driver.
